  "result": {
    "summary": "The Byzantine field army was broken and Romanos was captured, then released after about a week for a treaty and ransom. Doukas-faction intrigue deposed him; the civil wars that followed left Anatolia open to Turkish settlement. Modern historians stress the battle's political more than its material consequences.",
    "casualties": {
      "A": "Not recorded; probably light",
      "B": "Sources give ~2,000-8,000 killed and ~4,000 captured, with many more scattering; modern scholars think losses were lower than older accounts claimed"
    }
  },
